{"archetypes":[{"name":"ledger-schema","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan introduces a new timing-ledger row type and JSON substructure whose exact field contracts can drift across writer, parser, docs, and tests.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the proposed 13-column timing-ledger round rows and timing-report JSON rounds schema are fully specified against the existing ledger/report implementation and documented contracts. Look for field-order ambiguity, backward-compatibility gaps, escaping/sanitization mismatches, or parser assumptions that could make valid rows disappear or produce invalid JSON. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"deferred-handoff","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The hardest failure surface is deferred main-agent vote flow, where timing starts, counts, and ledger binding cross script/prompt boundaries.","prompt_body":"Focus on the deferred handoff paths for implement and design rounds, especially main-agent-vote-required and resumed Step 5 flows. Check whether the plan accounts for every transition needed to preserve round start time, bind the correct tmpdir ledger, avoid double-emission, and include prompt-side adjudication/apply/check/lint time in the round duration. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-freshness","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The acceptance depends on timing data reaching committed run logs, so stale or pre-rendered publish surfaces are a distinct plan-risk area.","prompt_body":"Review the plan-vs-evidence path from ledger rows to final timing-report JSON to larch-log batches for both implement and design. Look for missing render points, stale artifact hazards, ordering mistakes around design publishing, or assumptions that existing flush sites automatically pick up the richer report. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
